{"id":172,"name":"pichu","speciesId":172,"dex":172,"form":"normal","generation":2,"types":["electric"],"stats":{"hp":20,"attack":40,"defense":15,"special-attack":35,"special-defense":35,"speed":60},"abilities":[{"name":"static","hidden":false},{"name":"lightning-rod","hidden":true}],"height":3,"weight":20,"baseExp":41,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/172.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/172.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/172.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/172.ogg","genus":"Tiny Mouse Pokémon","genusPt":"Pequeno Pokémon Rato","flavor":[{"version":"gold","text":"It is not yet skilled at storing electricity. It may send out a jolt if amused or startled."},{"version":"silver","text":"Despite its small size, it can zap even adult humans. However, if it does so, it also surprises itself."},{"version":"crystal","text":"It is unskilled at storing electric power. Any kind of shock causes it to discharge energy spontaneously."},{"version":"ruby","text":"PICHU charges itself with electricity more easily on days with thunderclouds or when the air is very dry. You can hear the crackling of static electricity coming off this POKéMON."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"When PICHU plays with others, it may short out electricity with another PICHU, creating a shower of sparks. In that event, this POKéMON will begin crying, startled by the flash of sparks."},{"version":"emerald","text":"It is still inept at retaining electricity. When it is startled, it discharges power accidentally. It gets better at holding power as it grows older."},{"version":"diamond","text":"The electric pouches on its cheeks are still small. They cannot store much electricity yet."},{"version":"pearl","text":"It plays with others by touching tails and setting off sparks. This appears to be a test of courage."},{"version":"platinum","text":"The electric sacs in its cheeks are small. If even a little electricity leaks, it becomes shocked."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Pichu charges itself with electricity more easily on days with thunderclouds or when the air is very dry. You can hear the crackling of static electricity coming off this Pokémon."},{"version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"When Pichu plays with others, it may short out electricity with another Pichu, creating a shower of sparks. In that event, this Pokémon will begin crying, startled by the flash of sparks."},{"version":"sun","text":"It is not yet skilled at controlling electricity. If you take your eyes off it, it may shock itself."},{"version":"moon","text":"Despite this Pokémon’s cute appearance, those who want to live with one should prepare to be on the receiving end of its electric jolts."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"It still can’t use electricity well. When it’s surprised or excited, it discharges electricity unintentionally."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"It has electric sacs in its cheeks. When they’re fully charged, Pichu plays very energetically."},{"version":"legends-arceus","text":"Pichu stores electricity in the sacs on its cheeks but discharges it inadvertently when agitated or excited. Being yet immature, the Pokémon's handling of electricity is rather inept."}],"flavorPt":"Pichu armazena eletricidade nas bolsas em suas bochechas, mas a descarrega inadvertidamente quando está agitado ou excitado. Sendo ainda imaturo, o manejo da eletricidade do Pokémon é bastante inepto.","genderRate":4,"captureRate":190,"eggGroups":["no-eggs"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"pichu","speciesId":172,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Felicidade alta"],"species":"pikachu","speciesId":25,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Usar Thunder Stone","Usar Thunder Stone"],"species":"raichu","speciesId":26,"evolvesTo":[]}]}]},"v